  ('96452ec1-9b97-57b6-8ccf-00ce1a5a84af', 'f9a044d3-073d-5abf-b697-0f8d5f32b6e1', 'Lab 4: Binary Search Trees', '## Lab 4: Binary Search Trees

Implement a `BST` class in **main.py** that stores **unique integer keys**.

| Method | Expected behaviour |
|---|---|
| `insert(key)` | Insert `key`. **Duplicate keys must be ignored** (size stays the same). |
| `search(key) -> bool` | `True` if the key exists, else `False`. |
| `inorder() -> list[int]` | All keys in ascending order. |
| `min()` / `max()` | Smallest / largest key, or `None` for an empty tree. |
| `height() -> int` | Nodes on the longest root-to-leaf path (empty tree = `0`). |
| `len(tree)` | Number of keys stored. |

**Learning outcomes:** the BST ordering invariant, recursion vs. iteration, and edge cases
(empty trees, duplicates, skewed trees).

> Tip: press **Run Tests** often. If you get stuck, ask the **Socratic Tutor** — it will
> guide you with questions instead of handing you the answer.
', 'coding', 'python', '{"main.py": "class Node:\n    def __init__(self, key):\n        self.key = key\n        self.left = None\n        self.right = None\n\n\nclass BST:\n    \"\"\"Binary Search Tree that stores unique integer keys.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.root = None\n        self._size = 0\n\n    def insert(self, key):\n        # TODO: insert key while keeping the BST invariant (ignore duplicates)\n        pass\n\n    def search(self, key):\n        # TODO: return True if key exists\n        return False\n\n    def inorder(self):\n        # TODO: return keys in ascending order\n        return []\n\n    def min(self):\n        # TODO\n        return None\n\n    def max(self):\n        # TODO\n        return None\n\n    def height(self):\n        # TODO: empty tree has height 0\n        return 0\n\n    def __len__(self):\n        return self._size\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    tree = BST()\n    for k in [50, 30, 70, 20, 40, 60, 80]:\n        tree.insert(k)\n    print(\"Inorder:\", tree.inorder())\n    print(\"Height:\", tree.height())\n"}'::jsonb, '[{"name": "test_insert_and_search", "description": "Inserted keys are found; missing keys are not.", "hidden": false, "code": "t = BST()\nfor k in [50, 30, 70, 20, 40]:\n    t.insert(k)\nassert t.search(40) is True, \"search(40) should be True after inserting 40\"\nassert t.search(99) is False, \"search(99) should be False for a key that was never inserted\"", "inputs": null, "expected": null}, {"name": "test_inorder_traversal", "description": "inorder() returns keys in ascending order.", "hidden": false, "code": "t = BST()\nfor k in [50, 30, 70, 20, 40, 60, 80]:\n    t.insert(k)\nassert t.inorder() == [20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70, 80], f\"inorder() returned {t.inorder()}\"", "inputs": null, "expected": null}, {"name": "test_min_max", "description": "min()/max() work, and return None on an empty tree.", "hidden": false, "code": "t = BST()\nassert t.min() is None and t.max() is None, \"empty tree: min()/max() should return None\"\nfor k in [15, 6, 23, 4, 7, 71]:\n    t.insert(k)\nassert (t.min(), t.max()) == (4, 71), f\"expected (4, 71), got {(t.min(), t.max())}\"", "inputs": null, "expected": null}, {"name": "test_height", "description": "height() counts nodes on the longest path (empty = 0).", "hidden": false, "code": "t = BST()\nassert t.height() == 0, \"empty tree height should be 0\"\nfor k in [10, 5, 15, 3]:\n    t.insert(k)\nassert t.height() == 3, f\"expected height 3, got {t.height()}\"", "inputs": null, "expected": null}, {"name": "test_duplicate_keys", "description": "Inserting an existing key must not change the tree.", "hidden": false, "code": "t = BST()\nfor k in [8, 3, 10, 3, 8, 10]:\n    t.insert(k)\nassert len(t) == 3, f\"duplicates must be ignored: expected size 3, got {len(t)}\"\nassert t.inorder() == [3, 8, 10], f\"expected [3, 8, 10], got {t.inorder()}\"", "inputs": null, "expected": null}, {"name": "test_skewed_tree", "description": "Sorted insertion produces a skewed tree of height n.", "hidden": true, "code": "t = BST()\nfor k in range(1, 201):\n    t.insert(k)\nassert t.height() == 200, f\"expected height 200, got {t.height()}\"\nassert t.inorder() == list(range(1, 201))", "inputs": null, "expected": null}, {"name": "test_single_negative_key", "description": "Works with a single negative key.", "hidden": true, "code": "t = BST()\nt.insert(-5)\nassert t.inorder() == [-5] and t.height() == 1\nassert t.min() == t.max() == -5", "inputs": null, "expected": null}]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "correctness", "name": "Correctness", "description": "All BST operations behave as specified, including hidden tests.", "max_points": 5.0}, {"id": "edge_cases", "name": "Edge cases", "description": "Duplicates, empty tree and skewed trees handled.", "max_points": 2.0}, {"id": "code_quality", "name": "Code quality", "description": "Readable names, docstrings, no dead code or leftover TODOs.", "max_points": 2.0}, {"id": "efficiency", "name": "Efficiency", "description": "Operations run in O(h); no unnecessary full-tree scans.", "max_points": 1.0}]'::jsonb, 10.0, now() + interval '280800 seconds', 'published', true, 'exam', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ee361545-07d3-58c1-bf7f-9a0710703bd3', now() - interval '518400 seconds', now() - interval '518400 seconds'),
